@startuml
' Reference ticket lifecycle for a full agent fleet.
'
' This is a PATTERN, not this repo's instance. Derive your own from it and keep
' yours in sync in the same commit as any trigger or label-edge change.
'
' Read the edges as: who writes this transition. Exactly one automation owns
' each edge (.agents/automations/README.md § The rules). Reviewers own none.

title Ticket lifecycle — one writer per edge

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #333333
  FontName sans-serif
}
skinparam ArrowColor #555555

[*] --> needs_triage : issue created

state needs_triage as "needs-triage"
state needs_info as "needs-info"
state ready_for_agent as "ready-for-agent"
state agent_review as "agent-review"
state human_review as "human-review"
state ready_for_human as "ready-for-human"
state wontfix as "wontfix"
state Done

' ── triage-agent owns every edge out of needs-triage ────────────────────────
needs_triage --> ready_for_agent : **triage-agent**\nbrief written
needs_triage --> needs_info : **triage-agent**\nmissing information
needs_triage --> ready_for_human : **triage-agent**\nneeds human judgment
needs_triage --> wontfix : **triage-agent**
needs_info --> needs_triage : human answers

' ── implementer owns ready-for-agent → agent-review ─────────────────────────
ready_for_agent --> agent_review : **implementer**\nopens PR, links ticket

' ── reviewers comment, never label ──────────────────────────────────────────
state "PR open" as pr #EEEEEE {
  state "reviewer: correctness" as r1
  state "reviewer: structure" as r2
  state "reviewer: refactoring" as r3
  state "reviewer: spec" as r4
}
agent_review --> pr : pr-opened / pr-pushed\nfires every lens independently
pr --> agent_review : verdicts posted to the ledger\n(no label writes)

' ── review-verdict owns every edge out of agent-review ──────────────────────
agent_review --> ready_for_agent : **review-verdict**\nfindings to address
agent_review --> human_review : **review-verdict**\nlenses converged

' ── human-verdict owns every edge out of human-review ───────────────────────
human_review --> ready_for_agent : **human-verdict**\nchanges requested
human_review --> Done : **human-verdict**\nafter the *human* merges
human_review --> human_review : silence — untouched

ready_for_human --> Done : human does the work

note right of human_review
  **Automations never merge.**
  Their credentials must not
  carry merge rights.
end note

note bottom of pr
  Lenses are independent.
  No lens reads another's findings —
  the independence is the value.

  A joiner fires on every comment and
  acts only when all lenses have
  reported for the head sha.
end note

@enduml
